      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Figured it out. From the documentation https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/base-types/standard-numeric-format-strings : \n\"D\" or \"d\"\tDecimal\tResult: Integer digits with optional negative sign.\nSupported by: Integral types only.\nI thought since it was Decimal it needed a decimal format instead of float but it actually needs an Integer format.\nAfter changing the lower node to Convert ToInt32 it worked!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
